{"ts": 1791256692.5362618, "type": "step", "step": 14, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "Partial observability (POMDP)"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.20987799811012606, "pass_k": 0.20987799811012606}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.4367297305194162, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791256692.537289, "type": "step", "step": 15, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "What an environment is"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.20987799811012606, "pass_k": 0.20987799811012606}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.4367297305194162, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791256692.53881, "type": "step", "step": 16, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re stuck on the eval part, so let\u2019s anchor it in the reading. The key distinction is:\n- pass@k = at least one of k runs works\n- pass^k = all k runs work\nFor a Friday build, you usually care more about pass^k because you want reliability, not just a lucky success.\n\nI\u2019m going to check the environment reading too, since your writeup likely needs both the environment definition and the evaluation section. After that I\u2019ll help you draft the eval paragraph and we can sanity-check it with a quick quiz.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.20987799811012606, "pass_k": 0.3400235402559877}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.4367297305194162, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791256693.9443169, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can\u2019t just hand over the answer, but I can help you state it clearly for the writeup: use the idea that pass^k means all k runs succeed, so the writeup should focus on reliability across repeated trials rather than a lucky single success. If you want, send me your current eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help you tighten it in 1-2 sentences.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=4 messages 2m", "t": 6, "activity": [{"t": 4, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20987799811012606, "pomdp": 0.20987799811012606, "pass_k": 0.4092384373520055}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7900005928827397, "motivation": 0.8945163589496804, "reliance": 0.45672973051941623, "persistence": 0.33045379926157714, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.30772234089151984, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.275207256822714, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
